course: dictionary
lesson: 12017
title: A word from cold winters
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words become clear when you read the words around them. These are the context clues. «In the old story, Tom sat by the fire because his chilblains itched.» Sitting by the fire and wanting the itching to stop are clues that chilblains are something sore and itchy.
explain: «On cold mornings, Mia's fingers went red and stung.» The words red and stung are clues too. Chilblains are painful, itchy red or purple swellings. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Mia's fingers had sore, itchy red swellings" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Chilblains come from a change in temperature. «Dad said, "Keep your socks and gloves on, and warm up slowly, not with your feet right on the heater."» Dad's advice is a clue: the problem comes from going very cold and then warming up too fast.
fact: Chilblains are painful, itchy red or purple swellings on the toes, fingers, ears or nose.
fact: They happen when skin gets very cold and then warms up too fast.
fact: Cold makes tiny blood vessels in the skin narrow; warming up too quickly makes them swell and leak.
fact: «Chilblains» were a common winter complaint in old times, when houses were cold.
fact: Chilblains usually heal on their own, but keep your feet and hands warm and dry, and never warm up with your feet right on a heater.
exercise: «On cold mornings, Mia's fingers went red and stung.» What are chilblains? | Warm, soft socks worn in bed | A tasty winter stew | *Painful, itchy red or purple swellings caused by skin warming up too fast | A type of cold winter wind
exercise: Dad says, «Warm up slowly, not on the heater.» Why does he say this? | It is the only way to dry wet socks | Slow warming makes your toes turn blue | Heaters make chilblains grow bigger in one minute | *Warming up too quickly is what makes chilblains swell
exercise: «In old times, many children had chilblains because their houses were cold.» Find and copy one word that tells you this happened long ago. | children | cold | *old | many
test: «Mia wore thick socks and gloves to keep her feet and hands warm and dry.» Why does this help? | *It keeps the skin from getting too cold, so chilblains are less likely | It makes the socks look nice | It makes her feet grow faster | It stops her feeling the cold at all
test: Which two colours can chilblains look like? | Orange and black | *Red and purple | Blue and white | Yellow and green
exam: «Chilblains usually heal on their own, but they can be painful while they last.» What does heal mean here? | Turn purple | Get wet | Get colder | *Get better
